---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const blogPostingSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BlogPosting",
  "headline": "Community Spotlight: Minister Will Groom — \"Keep God First\"",
  "description": "Community Spotlight on Minister Will Groom of Shelby, NC — shot over 24 times on December 14, 1993 and survived. A story of faith, resilience, and keeping God first.",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Shelby Web Company", "url": "https://www.shelbywebco.com" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Shelby Web Company", "logo": { "@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://www.shelbywebco.com/og-image.jpg" } },
  "mainEntityOfPage": "https://www.shelbywebco.com/blog/minister-will-groom-keep-god-first-spotlight/"
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Community Spotlight: Minister Will Groom — 'Keep God First'"
  description="Community Spotlight on Minister Will Groom of Shelby, NC — shot over 24 times on December 14, 1993 and survived. A story of faith, resilience, and keeping God first."
>
  <script is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(blogPostingSchema)} type="application/ld+json"></script>
  <article class="pt-24 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <header class="mb-10 text-center">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 mb-6 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-[#c9a86a]/20 bg-[#c9a86a]/5">
          <span class="text-[#c9a86a] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Community Spotlight</span>
          <span class="w-1 h-1 rounded-full bg-[#c9a86a]/30"></span>
          <span class="text-white/90 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest">September 2026</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-heading text-5xl md:text-7xl font-black text-white mb-8 tracking-tight leading-[1.1]">
          Community Spotlight: Minister Will Groom <br />
          <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-cyan to-brand-blue">"Keep God First"</span>
        </h1>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Some neighbors you just click with. The kind where the first conversation feels like you've known each other for years. That's exactly how it went when I met my new neighbor Will Groom — or as many know him, Minister Will Groom.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Will's the kind of guy who greets you with a genuine smile, carries himself with quiet confidence, and looks like he's in better shape than most people half his age. He's warm, he's engaging, and he's the type of neighbor who reminds you why community matters.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          But here's the thing about Will — if he hadn't told me his story, I never would have believed it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">December 14, 1993: A Night That Should Have Changed Everything</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          On December 14, 1993, at 10:30 PM, Will was outside when he was approached by a random assailant. What happened next is the kind of story you hear about on the news and think, "Nobody walks away from that."
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Will was shot over 24 times.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Let that sink in. Not once. Not twice. Over 24 times.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          And he survived.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          When Will's girlfriend shared this with me, I was stunned for a minute to let it sink in. Because looking at him today — healthy, strong, full of life — you would never, ever guess that he endured something so traumatic. There's no visible scar that tells the story. His foot did get paralyzed. And it's amazing because he walks around just fine. No outward sign of the battle he fought. Just a man standing before you, alive and well, as if the laws of probability decided to make an exception.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          But Will will tell you it wasn't luck. It wasn't chance. And it definitely wasn't a coincidence.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">The Man Behind the Miracle</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          What strikes you most about Will isn't just what he survived — it's who he became because of it. He didn't let that night define him in bitterness or fear. Instead, he emerged with a message, a calling, and a purpose that he's carried ever since.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Today, Minister Will Groom lives by a simple, powerful motto:
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-center">
          "Keep God first."
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          That's it. Three words. But when you know what he's been through, those three words carry the weight of a lifetime. They aren't just a catchphrase — they're a testimony. A philosophy forged in the darkest moment imaginable and refined through decades of living proof that faith, resilience, and divine purpose can carry you through what should have been the end.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">Why Will's Story Matters to Shelby</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          In a world that often feels divided and disconnected, Will Groom is a reminder that the people living right next door have stories that can stop you in your tracks. He's a reminder that survival isn't just about making it through — it's about what you do after.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Will's presence in our community is a gift. He's proof that no matter what you've been through, you can still show up for your neighbors. You can still smile. You can still share wisdom. You can still keep God first.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8">A Neighbor Worth Knowing</h2>
        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          If you ever get the chance to meet Minister Will Groom, take it. Ask him about his faith. Ask him about his journey. And most importantly, listen to what he has to say — because this is a man who has earned every word.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          In Shelby, NC, we're surrounded by incredible people building incredible businesses. But every now and then, we meet someone who reminds us that the most important thing we can build isn't a brand or a website — it's a life grounded in something bigger than ourselves.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          Keep God first.
        </p>

        <p class="text-white mb-8 leading-relaxed">
          That's Will's message. And after hearing his story, it really coins the message that much further.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-[#c9a86a] to-brand-darkest p-10 rounded-[2rem] text-center relative overflow-hidden my-12">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_50%_50%,rgba(201,168,106,0.15),transparent_70%)]"></div>
          <p class="text-white text-xl md:text-2xl font-medium relative z-10">
            Have someone in the Shelby, NC community who deserves the spotlight? <a href="/contact/" class="underline hover:text-brand-darkest transition-colors">Reach out to us</a> — we'd love to share their story.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 p-8 bg-brand-dark/50 border border-white/5 rounded-2xl">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">More Community Spotlights</h2>
        <div class="space-y-2 text-white/90">
          <p>Read more about the people and businesses keeping our region strong: <a href="/blog/building-people-not-just-buildings-james-richardson-spotlight/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">James Brinson Richardson</a>, <a href="/blog/support-first-responders-spotlight/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Supporting Local First Responders</a>, and <a href="/blog/reflections-paint-body-works-spotlight/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">Reflections Paint & Body Works</a>.</p>
          <p class="mt-4">About the author: David Richardson — Founder / Lead Developer, Shelby Web Company. We're your local <a href="/services/web-design/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">web design</a> and <a href="/services/seo/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline">SEO</a> agency serving Cleveland County, NC. When we're not building websites, we're building community — one story at a time.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <footer class="mt-24 pt-12 border-t border-white/5 flex flex-wrap gap-8 items-center justify-between">
        <a href="/blog/" class="text-white/90 hover:text-white transition-colors flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>
          Back to Blog
        </a>
        <div class="flex gap-6">
          <a href="/" class="text-white/90 hover:text-white transition-colors">Home</a>
          <a href="/about/" class="text-white/90 hover:text-white transition-colors">About Us</a>
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-white/90 hover:text-white transition-colors">Contact</a>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
